## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates knowledge of edge ML deployment, covering model optimization, over-the-air updates, and monitoring strategies for resource-constrained environments.

## Key Concepts
- Edge inference using SageMaker Edge Manager
- Model quantization (INT8) for ARM64 architecture
- OTA updates via AWS IoT Jobs with rollback slots
- Local telemetry and validation with intermittent connectivity

## Code Example
```javascript
// Model inference with latency tracking
const model = loadModel('arm_int8.tflite');
const t0 = performance.now();
const output = model.run(input);
const latency = performance.now() - t0;

// Emit telemetry for edge agent
emitTelemetry({ latency, outputQuality: evaluateQuality(output) });
```

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to design multi-region, residency-compliant ML deployments combining real-time and batch workloads, governance, and automated rollback. Tests practical use of SageMaker Endpoint Variants, Model Registry, and drift tooling.

## Key Concepts

- Regional real-time endpoints with VPC isolation
- Per-region Feature Store governance
- Batch Transform for analytics
- Model Registry versioning
- Drift detection with Clarify
- Canary rollouts and automated rollback
- Cost controls and autoscaling

## Code Example

```javascript
// CDK deployment pattern for regional ML infrastructure
const modelPackage = new sagemaker.CfnModelPackage(this, 'ModelPackage', {
  modelPackageName: modelVersion.name,
  approvalStatus: 'Approved',
  sourceAccount: process.env.AWS_ACCOUNT_ID
